# Lab 05 – Implement Intersite Connectivity

## Objectives  
- Establish connectivity between Azure virtual networks (VNets) using VPN gateways.  
- Configure site-to-site VPN connections.  
- Test traffic flow between remote networks.

## Tasks Completed  
- Created resource group **az104-rg5** (or the lab’s designated RG).  
- Deployed two VNets (e.g. `az104-vnet1`, `az104-vnet2`) with appropriate address spaces and subnets.  
- Created **VPN gateways** in each VNet (e.g. `az104-vnet1-gw`, `az104-vnet2-gw`).  
- Configured **local network gateways** for on-prem or remote network definitions.  
- Set up **site-to-site VPN connections** between the gateways.  
- Verified connectivity by sending network traffic (ping, etc.) across the VPN link.

## Key Takeaways  
- VPN gateways enable encrypted connectivity between VNets or between on-premises and Azure.  
- Local network gateway objects represent the remote network in Azure.  
- Site-to-site connections allow resources in different VNets to communicate as if local.

